 on the  podcast i have to ask about this tweet  and it was jeff lewis talking about the  midas list okay and he said uh talk  about keith's boy while he's likely to  be on the mice list this year that  hasn't been on it for the past two to  three years speaks volumes about their  methodology and you followed up and said  i had a pretty good year too eight exits  you name the companies but none of them  count because it was my own money  so i kept 100 percent instead of 20  which they don't like whatever  and  forget the minus list stuff and kind of  debate there for a second uh  those eight companies exiting you're the  individual investor it's your money uh  whatever the math is they were starting  small they ended up being big  how do you manage your own money like  are you just all in startups and that's  like pretty much what you're doing do  you have stocks do you do real estate do  you buy you know local businesses and  david sax's funding you know the the gas  station down the street like what do you  do or what's your approach  so um i mean i generally do it myself  and i mean there's an old saying which  is uh concentrate to get rich diversify  to stay rich so we are all if you're  doing a startup you're highly  concentrated like i'm saying in this  venture  and i think what you want to do is if  you're lucky enough to be successful you  want to diversify so that  you know  you can go down with the market but  you're not a position to lose everything  you know  and so i don't do anything exotic you  know it's the short answer is i'm pretty  diversified  uh and that's like diversification it's  just like you're buying a low cost index  type stuff or are you yeah i mean i try  to yeah i mean i'm not like a huge  public market stock picker i generally  just buy  indices for the most like vanguard funds  type stuff  i do some commercial real estate  investing um probably because you know i  like it it's fun  um but remember you know most of the  investing i do is actually through craft  you know and i also write large gp  checks to craft so i'm doing i'm getting  that exposure already  and so i'm not trying to do anything  like overly aggressive in my own  portfolio because  i'm really just focused on you know  investing the right startups yeah it's  um it's always fascinating to me right  like the amount of risk it takes to  build companies and then to then  basically have to turn that off in terms  of managing the rest uh goes counter to  you know the dna of many of these people  uh and so hearing you you know imagining  you buying low cost indexes and then the  famous story of elon be like well i had  180 million dollars and i basically  spent it all right like it is uh uh very  interesting well part of it is that  it's part of it is time and attention as  well as risk so i want my time and  attention to be where actually hopefully  i have like an advantage as an investor  which is in the startup ecosystem and  it's very time consuming to work with  these companies to be picking all that  kind of stuff i don't want to be  spending my time trying to figure out an  active strategy  you know i'm saying i'm like i don't  want to read the quarterly reports of  all these companies i mean i'm not  saying there's anything wrong with doing  that it's just i personally  don't want to spend the time to do it so  i want to implement easy strategies i'm  imagining you sitting there day trading  from your desk  i've never been never been a day trader  um so yeah i mean  yeah got it um my last question is one  of our sponsors is eight sleep and uh  they've got the thermo-regulated bed um  walk us just through like a day in your  life slash like diet sleep like just how  do you try to optimize your life to be  able to do all the things that you're  doing yeah i'm an investor in a sleep  it's a great product i really like it so  am i yeah so you sleep on one then yeah  yeah yeah yeah i just make it so yeah no  no i think it's great um